    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test in the project, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced the `@Transient getMembershipTier()` (GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) with `getMembershipLevel()`, which computes the level as a derived field: starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, and `Math.min(level, 3)` to cap at 3 (leaving 4 reserved for tenure).\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed the `membershipTier` string property from the Owner response schema and added `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1, max 3, `readOnly`). The generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` pick this up automatically by name-matching, so `getMembershipLevel()` \u2192 `membershipLevel` in the response.\n\n3. **`repository/OwnerRepository.java`** \u2014 Updated a doc comment that referenced \"assigning its membership tier\" (the household-size sizing that fed the old GOLD tier) so it no longer refers to the removed concept.\n\nNotes on the spec's other hints:\n- The **create audit line** (`OwnerAuditLogger.logCreated`) records id/customerCode/registrationDate but never recorded the tier, so there was nothing to convert there \u2014 no code in the codebase recorded the old tier value.\n- `householdSize` (the old GOLD input) is still a persisted column populated at creation, so I left that computation untouched \u2014 it's outside the scope of this change.\n\n`GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `membershipLevel` instead of `membershipTier`, and the acceptance test (unique owner with email \u2192 level 3) passes, with the full build green.",
